MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Picks' why line (web PicksFeed, list rows, welcome tour; iPhone PicksScreen,
BrowseListRow, WelcomeTour) says the rating verb of the lowest-rated film it
names, via lib/rating-verb.ts (whyLineVerb / pickWhyAnchors; iPhone WhyVerb).
/api/pick-why sends each film's verb and names loved (4.5★+) anchors first,
keeping 4★ anchors when no loved one is close. The reveal line, its proof
lead-in and the Taste Mixes anchor lane take their films' verb too. The
notification switch is renamed "Friends who rated it highly too" on web and
iPhone Settings; detail and threshold unchanged. Web why cache bumped to
montage_why:v2. Invariant 1620 added; 220, 234, 458, 719, 1337, 1412, 1501,
1567 amended. Swift not compiled here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013WRDCFXH8nihP92apJAVW7
